{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1100730-treasure-question","id":1100730,"title":"Treasure question...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-06T00:02:16-07:00","id":1100730,"title":"Treasure question...","content":"My players are creating Treasures and we have a question.<br /> <br /> If you roll to activate the item, either Glamour or Int. + Gremayre is the difficulty: 8?<br /> <br /> That seems fairly hefty since you can't do a bunk?<br /> <br /> I'm considering lowering the difficulty to 6...<br /> <br /> or<br /> <br /> Reducing the difficulty by the rating of the treasure...<br /> <br /> From the perspective of people not knee deep in city creation will either of these work?<br /> <br /> Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1383-yrtalien","name":"yrtalien","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T20:57:54-07:00","id":1115365,"title":"","content":"I think it depends on the treasure. In the games I run most of the time I make it a simple case of &quot;spend a point of Glamour, activate the Treasure&quot;. Since Glamour is so precious, the PCs won't be doing it all of the time, and it prevents us from having to worry about the difficulty of a roll. I've done this method for so many years I can't remember if the canon books require a roll for activation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://imgbb.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://image.ibb.co/fzeOgQ/1172c70f3ff188688852c74c8145285c_original_2_4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> Visit my freehold for Changeling links, settings, art, and other goodies.<br /> <a href=\"https://theshepherdsfreehold.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The Shepherd's Freehold</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13648-shepherd","name":"Shepherd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T08:59:28-07:00","id":1115966,"title":"","content":"Treasures have never been very clear. They're still not now. You might make the difficulty equal to your own Banality, modified by how appropriate their use of the Treasure is. If they're attacking a really Banal target, the difficulty might be their Banality instead. For most fae, that means using a Treasure is easy, but it's harder for the Enchanted or when you're using it on Autumn Person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T06:10:19-07:00","id":1116344,"title":"","content":"I have never considered that you need to roll any Trait or spend Glamour in order to activate a Treasure. Never was it said in the previous editions. Treasures were so precious an valuable because they were naturally enchanted items, potent with Glamour and the enchantments of the Dreaming, and so could affect even non-enchanted humans, enchanting them (as Saint Michael pointed out in the thread on the kinain, p. 147 of C:tD 2nd ed.).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","user":"mattboggan","date":". 07-15-2017, 09:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","name":"mattboggan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T08:55:15-07:00","id":1116851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mattboggan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1100730-treasure-question?p=1116344#post1116344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have never considered that you need to roll any Trait or spend Glamour in order to activate a Treasure. Never was it said in the previous editions. Treasures were so precious an valuable because they were naturally enchanted items, potent with Glamour and the enchantments of the Dreaming, and so could affect even non-enchanted humans, enchanting them (as Saint Michael pointed out in the thread on the kinain, p. 147 of C:tD 2nd ed.).</div> </div> </div> </div>But some effects of Treasures specifically require a roll. In Second Edition, it was specifically written that a Treasure emulates a single Art. So, winged boots might emulate Quicksilver. If so, however, you'd need a roll to determine how many extra actions you get. And then what do you roll? Your Glamour? Your own Art + Realm?<br /> <br /> So, either Glamour or Intelligence + Gremayre makes sense. But the difficulty is never stated anywhere. Difficulty 8 seems too high. You could just assume difficulty 6, I guess...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T10:27:59-07:00","id":1116890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1100730-treasure-question?p=1116851#post1116851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But some effects of Treasures specifically require a roll. In Second Edition, it was specifically written that a Treasure emulates a single Art. So, winged boots might emulate Quicksilver. If so, however, you'd need a roll to determine how many extra actions you get. And then what do you roll? Your Glamour? Your own Art + Realm?<br /> <br /> So, either Glamour or Intelligence + Gremayre makes sense. But the difficulty is never stated anywhere. Difficulty 8 seems too high. You could just assume difficulty 6, I guess...</div> </div> </div> </div>If I ran into a situation like this I'd make a roll like a regular cantrip, and make a standard difficulty of 6 (since treasures are supposed to be powerful). But in my games I'm more specific about the functions of treasures, so in the example of the winged boots I'd have it give a specific number of extra actions per activation. <br /> <br /> One of my PCs had a treasure that was a ring which could see the past of any object. By touching the ring to the object they could see what happened to and around it over the object's history. In that case I did make them roll. They would spend a point of Glamour to activate it and then roll their current Glamour rating to see how far back and how clear the visions were. Then I used my storyteller license to give them as much or as little information as I really wanted them to have.<br /> <br /> In another case a character had a sword that would light up covered with flame. After spending a point of Glamour the sword would do an extra 3 dice of fire damage. Though it mimicked and effect of Pyretics, I didn't have any roll to see how much damage it did with each activation. It also made more sense for a treasure to always do the same damage rather than a highly variable amount.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://imgbb.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://image.ibb.co/fzeOgQ/1172c70f3ff188688852c74c8145285c_original_2_4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> Visit my freehold for Changeling links, settings, art, and other goodies.<br /> <a href=\"https://theshepherdsfreehold.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The Shepherd's Freehold</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13648-shepherd","name":"Shepherd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}